<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's monetary base up 7.16 pct in wk to Dec 6.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's monetary base up 7.16 pct in wk to Dec 6.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base grew 7.16 percent to 2.91 billion sucres in the week to December 6, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>The bank did not give any reason for the increase.</p>
<p>In November, the monetary base fell 1.05 percent to 2.72 billion sucres.</p>
<p>The monetary base ended 1995 at 2.41 billion sucres, up from 1.85 billion sucres at the end of 1994.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
</text>
